# Freqtrade rules
config*.json
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-shm
*.sqlite-wal
logfile.txt
user_data/*
!user_data/strategy/sample_strategy.py
!user_data/notebooks
!user_data/models
!user_data/freqaimodels
user_data/freqaimodels/*
user_data/models/*
user_data/notebooks/*

# ── OUR DELIVERED STRATEGIES MUST NEVER BE SILENTLY EXCLUDED ────────────────
# `user_data/*` above excludes the whole tree, which means it also excluded
# user_data/strategies/ and user_data/strategies_frontier/. That is how the
# deployed strategies nearly went uncommitted a second time: docs-myself was
# never tracked either, and when the workspace was lost twice there was no git
# copy to restore from. `git add` reported nothing wrong; the files were simply
# ignored, and the only symptom was a clean-looking `git status`.
# These two lines make the strategies ordinary tracked source code again, so
# plain `git add -A` is enough and no one has to remember `git add -f`.
!user_data/strategies/
!user_data/strategies_frontier/
#
# NOT re-included, on purpose. These are enforced rules, not a comment: a
# comment that reads like a guard is worse than no guard. See
# EXCLUDED_FROM_VCS.md for the file-by-file list and the reason for each.
# Nothing here has been deleted; every file is still on disk.
docs-myself/Note-From-Wechat.pdf
docs-myself/_xref_pdfs/
docs-myself/_xref_pdfs
tools/carry/docs/
tools/carry/docs
tools/carry/_doc/
tools/carry/_doc
tools/carry/_src/
tools/carry/_src
tools/carry/*.pdf
tools/carry/*.csv.gz
tmp_audit/*.pdf
tmp_audit/redteam/*.pdf
tmp_paper/*.pdf
protocols.json
#
# TRADING CONFIGS STAY EXCLUDED (`config*.json`, above). The deployed configs
# hold exchange API credentials - currently empty, but that is the one file type
# where an empty string today becomes a real key tomorrow. Their full field list
# is documented in docs-myself/DELIVERABLE_SPEC_2026-09-30.md section 3.
freqtrade-plot.html
freqtrade-profit-plot.html
freqtrade/rpc/api_server/ui/*
build_helpers/ta-lib/*

